   axis: the layer has no physical pixel there, so no attachment of the map's physical size can be
   made, and what Metal rasterizes in such a pass is not measured.
+
+
+An explicit kernel imageblock uses the larger of its declared data size and the widest bounded access through a cell pointer, rounded to its alignment. Loads, stores, atomics and texture slice writes determine that reach; accesses before the cell or without a bound keep their existing refusal checks. An explicit layout aliased onto an implicit imageblock retains the declared cell.
